#X text 240 83 A non-interpolating sound generator based on the Gingerbreadman
map \, a two-dimensional discrete dynamical system. Unlike interpolating
generators that produce a continuous stream of values \, this object
advances the map by one step per audio sample at a given generation
frequency. The generation frequency is set as an audio signal on the
inlet; the minimal value is 0.001 Hz.;
#X text 240 214 The map is defined by the difference equations:;
#X text 240 239 x(n+1) = 1 - y(n) + |x(n)|;
#X text 240 264 y(n+1) = x(n);
#X text 240 289 For most initial values (x \, y) the sequence of points
(x(n) \, y(n)) traces a bounded \, non-repeating orbit with a characteristic
"gingerbread man" shape. Typical initial values that put the generator
into the chaotic region are x = 1.2 and y = 2.1 (the defaults).;
#X obj 240 377 ui.link @background_color 0.90196 0.90196 0.90196
@title wiki: Gingerbreadman map @url
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gingerbreadman_map;
